    "result_text": "The test passes and the build succeeds. The only test class in the suite is `AcceptanceTest` (the others are an abstract base and a helper), so the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `RejectDuplicateHousehold`/`RejectDuplicateTelephone` steps), I added:\n\n- **`RejectCityAtCapacity`** (`.../function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners with a matching city (case-insensitive, trimmed) via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`; throws the checked `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the owner being created isn't counted.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) and its global handler **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`**, which responds 409 (`CONFLICT`) with a `ProblemDetail` body, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n- The escalation YAML `officefloor/escalation/...CityAtCapacityException.yml`.\n- Wired the new `rejectCityAtCapacity` step into `owners.POST.yml` (after `rejectDuplicateHousehold`, before `assignHousehold`), with `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
